cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself
  and the accompanying paper.
type: software
title: >-
  UNIQAT: UNderwater Image QUality Assessment Toolkit
abstract: >-
  Open-source Python package for automated, reference-free
  underwater image quality assessment. UNIQAT computes 37
  image quality metrics across nine categories (colour cast,
  contrast, sharpness, feature richness, visibility, turbidity,
  underwater-specific IQA, information content, and usability)
  and combines them into task-specific composite quality
  scores suitable for reef imaging, marine surveys, and
  underwater computer vision applications. The toolkit
  provides a command-line interface, a Python API, a Gradio
  web application, SLURM job scripts for HPC deployment, and
  optional deep learning models for fast metric approximation.
